Bitemporal records (PostgreSQL only). DNSZone, DNSRegistration, and all DNS record types now track two time axes: `valid_during` (when the fact was true in the world) and `recorded_during` (when Nautobot believed it). Calling `obj.save()` on an existing row with changed tracked fields rotates the belief log: the prior row's `recorded_during` window is closed and a new row with a fresh `entry_id` is inserted. The default manager filters to current beliefs; `Model.all_versions.as_of(<dt>)` returns the point-in-time view. New REST extensions: `?as_of=<iso8601>` on list endpoints and `GET /<id>/history/` for the per-record audit trail. MySQL deployments retain the previous schema and behavior; the 0008 migration is a no-op on non-Postgres backends. See `docs/user/feature_bitemporal.md`.
